 for being the first person to say yes to a slightly ridiculous plan. More adventures this year, please.","From Lee: Your emergency snack drawer has saved more afternoons than you know. Today the cake is on us.","From Pat: You make new people feel like they have always belonged here. That is a rare thing. Happy birthday.","From Alex: I was told to keep this short, so: best teammate, excellent friend, questionable karaoke choices. Never change."],tip:"Collect messages by chat or email and paste each one into a note. Contributors do not edit the card themselves. Four notes require the optional Boost upgrade.",relatedPath:"/group-birthday-card",relatedLabel:"How group birthday cards work"},{id:"dad",title:"A very unofficial award for Dad",description:"A cheerful card celebrating the jokes, the advice and the little things.",recipient:"Dad",sender:"Charlie",templateId:"confetti-pop",message:"Happy birthday, Dad. Your jokes are still terrible, your directions still involve landmarks that no longer exist, and you are still the first person I call when I need help. Thank you for showing up, every time.",notes:["This year's unofficial award: Most Likely to Fix It with Something Already in the Garage. No competition. Unanimous decision.","One thing I do not say enough: I learned what being dependable looks like by watching you. I am grateful for that."],tip:"Make the pretend award about a real habit. It is a simple text note, so this example stays within the free two-surprise limit.",relatedPath:"/birthday-card-for-dad",relatedLabel:"Birthday cards for Dad"},{id:"last-minute",title:"Short, warm, and ready to send",description:"One good message and a birthday promise, with a free classic design.",recipient:"Taylor",sender:"Alex",templateId:"classic",message:"Happy birthday, Taylor! I hope today has your favourite people, something delicious, and at least one moment you wish you could bottle. You deserve a lovely day and a year full of good surprises.",notes:["Birthday IOU: on